{"availability":"available","full":"typegoose/mongodb-memory-server","name":"mongodb-memory-server","description":"Manage & spin up mongodb server binaries with zero(or slight) configuration for tests.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2852,"forks":191,"created":"2017-05-11T18:32:46Z","updated":"2026-09-22T14:41:07Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://typegoose.github.io/mongodb-memory-server/","topics":["mock","mongodb","mongoose","testing","testing-tools","tests"],"demo":"https://typegoose.github.io/mongodb-memory-server/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:26:23.608Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:26:23.608Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:26:23.608Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:36:45.868Z","stars":2853,"forks":191},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:26:23.608Z","stars":2852,"forks":191}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[]( []( []( []( []( []( [](#backers) [](#sponsors) [](","This package spins up an actual/real MongoDB server programmatically from within nodejs, for testing or mocking during development. By default it holds the data in memory. A fresh spun up mongod process takes about 7Mb of memory. The server will allow you to connect your favorite ODM or client library to the MongoDB server and run integration tests isolated from each other.","On install, this package downloads the latest MongoDB binaries and saves them to a cache folder. (only mongodb-memory-server-core does not download on postinstall)"],"features":["Choose the Correct Package","Configuring which mongod binary to use","Available options for MongoMemoryServer","Available options for MongoMemoryReplSet","Simple test with MongoClient in Jest"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/typegoose/mongodb-memory-server/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"c0b998a57c9e55cbd4fd31d629510ad2c5e17aebde21f4e5d0c80ed7f9a04259","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:46.084Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03: